[
    {
        "text": "How does a DAO work? Token holders of a particular project can vote on issues that must be decided. The voting power is distributed generally based on the number of tokens users hold. The decisions to be voted on are written as proposals in smart contracts, and users must select between mutually exclusive options. After token holders vote and based on the outcome of the votes, the smart contracts are automatically executed to implement the decision. Some issues that token holders vote on include whether to issue more tokens, whether transactions transaction fees should increase, or whether a certain number of tokens should be burnt. A token burn means taking tokens out of circulation permanently. A crypto investment DAO's token holders might vote on which investment strategy to use. A sociopolitical DAO's token holders may vote on how the funds in the DAO will be dispersed and for what purposes.",
        "start": 400,
        "end": 53660,
        "confidence": 0.98834205,
        "channel": null,
        "speaker": "A",
